WEBVTT

00:08:29.658 --> 00:08:33.723
you can see why Marcus Books
has survived all these years.

00:08:34.325 --> 00:08:38.224
One person wrote that we have
a duty to preserve gems like this

00:08:38.248 --> 00:08:39.679
in our community.

00:08:40.599 --> 00:08:41.907
Someone else said,

00:08:41.931 --> 00:08:44.646
"I've been going to Marcus Books
since I was a child,

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:48.100
and Blanche Richardson
showed me many kindnesses."

00:08:49.266 --> 00:08:50.904
"Gems."

00:08:50.928 --> 00:08:52.476
"Kindnesses."

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:55.820
Those aren't words about technology.

00:08:55.844 --> 00:08:57.874
They're not even words about books.

00:08:58.474 --> 00:09:00.066
They're words about people.